    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d14">

                <pb facs="0099" n="11" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg11"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.G Personnel/39: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Uruguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wright</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-08-28T12:00:00-03:30">August 28,
                        1933—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 1:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>27. For the Secretary. The Foreign Office has telegraphically directed
                        Varela<anchor n="17" xml:id="d14-f1"/> to express the hope that you may head
                    our delegation to the forthcoming Conference and to intimate that affirmative
                    decision by you would undoubtedly result in attendance by other Foreign
                    Ministers and contribute greatly to the importance of the meeting.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wright</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d14-f1" n="17" xml:id="d14-f1-content">
                <p>J. Varela, Uruguayan Minister in the United States.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
